  "summary_en": "Korea's AI Framework Act (as amended January 2026) sets an AI master plan, a Presidential AI Council, and an AI Safety Institute. It imposes duties on operators of high-impact and generative AI: transparency notices, risk management, human oversight, and safety for large-compute models. It also provides industry promotion measures and administrative fines up to 30 million won.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines high-impact AI across energy, healthcare, medical devices, transport, biometrics, hiring and public decisions",
   "Operators must notify users of generative or high-impact AI and label generative outputs",
   "High-compute AI requires lifecycle risk management and reporting to the Minister of Science and ICT",
   "High-impact AI operators must provide risk management, explanation, user protection and human oversight",
   "Overseas operators must designate a domestic representative; fines up to 30 million won"
  ],
